00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:03.240
Rewarding your dog with a treat because it rolled over? Operant conditioning.

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:08.180
Giving your sex slave a new laptop because she survived a flogging? Operant conditioning.

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:10.080
CinemaSins: Expecting a sin every time you hear this ding?

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:10.580
*CinemaSins' "Ding!"*

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:11.620
CinemaSins: Operant conditioning.

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:14.340
Which leads to step 8, the final phase:

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:17.940
Controlling the recruit's identity, information, and environment.

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:23.140
All these other steps are how the person gets sucked in, but this is how the cult keeps them in,

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:27.000
isolating them from friends and family, 
changing the recruit's name,

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:30.840
randomly alternating between praise and love and scorn and punishment,

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:36.560
removing the recruits ability to choose by controlling things, like money, food, and career.

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:41.660
And notice that Grey has been doing all of these things the entire time.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:45.540
From the first moments of the movie, Anastasia repeatedly corrects Christian,

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:49.020
saying to call her Ana instead of Anastasia.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:53.220
He willfully ignores this, continuing to call her by her full name.

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:56.320
At the coffee shop, he gives her the muffin and tells her to eat.

00:15:56.320 --> 00:16:00.560
And again a few scenes later,  there are the "Eat this" and "Drink this" cards.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:04.360
When it comes to alternating between praise and punishment, he appears interested in Ana

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:09.720
in the coffee shop, but then rushes out to keep her off balance, punishing her for no fault of her own.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:15.920
By buying her new clothes, computers, and cars, Anastasia's financial independence is virtually gone.

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:20.680
Grey is even so "generous" as to get rid of her old car for her.

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:26.180
And at the bar, like the fifth scene in the movie, he physically removes Anastasia from the party,

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:32.020
blocking out longtime friend Jose, and having his brother run interference on her best friend Kate,

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:36.600
taking Anastasia to a place he deems appropriate when, let's face it, there was zero

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:40.620
reason for him to insert himself into that situation in the first place,

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:44.620
let alone bring her anywhere other than her own apartment.

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:50.860
He's already isolating her in the first 30 minutes of the movie, shaping her identity and managing her resources

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:56.100
like the good cult leader that he is. But then things take on a whole new meaning once she's inside the

00:16:56.100 --> 00:17:01.200
happy little love nest. Cult members are told what to eat, what to wear, when to sleep.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:05.700
And look where Anastasia is: her schedule is dictated by his demands.

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:11.680
When he tells her to, she must do her hair in a ponytail, and wait for him kneeling by the door,

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:17.220
hands just so. The contract requires that she only eat foods from a certain list.

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:22.700
And when she seeks an escape, needs to clear her head with the help of her family back in Georgia, because,

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:25.340
you know, some of this she might need to talk to someone about,

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:27.920
who's there to interrupt? I bet you can guess.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:29.400
Christian Grey.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:31.300
How romantic.

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:34.800
But hey, that's just a theory!

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:37.800
A Film Theory!
And...

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:40.360
CinemaSins: Host doesn't give special guests signature closing line.

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:41.980
Well then, go for it.

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:45.420
CinemaSins: OK then, that's just a theory, a film theory. Thanks for watching.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:48.440
Special guest ruins closing line by saying it too quickly!

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:49.420
Ding!

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:53.740
Hey, you just survived a 16 minute long video about 50 Shades of Grey!

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:56.680
So I must be doing something right here. Might as well subscribe!

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:59.900
Speaking of your life 16 minutes ago, remember that cold-open?

